1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:04,408
Ever notice the candy is always right next to the register? That's no accident.

2
00:00:04,658 --> 00:00:07,623
Food companies treat the checkout like prime real estate.

3
00:00:08,123 --> 00:00:12,923
Everyone has to pass the checkout to pay. And most of us wait in line, with nothing to do.

4
00:00:13,173 --> 00:00:18,080
So you stand there, bored, staring at chocolate at eye level. And at your kid's eye level too.

5
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:23,295
When some British supermarkets took the candy away from the checkout, shoppers bought less of it.

6
00:00:23,545 --> 00:00:27,470
About seventeen percent fewer grab-and-go sweets and chips, a year later.

7
00:00:27,720 --> 00:00:33,267
And one study of checkouts found about seventy percent of the food and drinks within reach was unhealthy.

8
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:38,204
Here's a twist: one industry survey found fewer impulse buys at self-checkout.

9
00:00:38,454 --> 00:00:41,313
Maybe because you're busy scanning, not staring at chocolate.

10
00:00:41,813 --> 00:00:45,333
So Tony tried a fruit bowl by his register. Nobody touched it.

11
00:00:45,583 --> 00:00:47,737
Then he tried a cookie jar. Gone by lunch.

12
00:00:48,237 --> 00:00:51,501
Next time: why stores play slow music. That's part four.

13
00:00:51,751 --> 00:00:55,741
Until then, when you're stuck in line, remember: that candy was put there for you.

